uid "3e56b548-f823-5efc-89ba-5bfa7fe486df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435814} :answer-field/id #uuid "a66e7a5d-9617-5080-a5e0-b50e86007465" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435823}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bdc664-5423-57fc-a753-871b318d24e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-34598" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that  $4a+3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -27 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2-(-9)=11.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119847 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119661 :question/id #uuid "7cce27e9-e2b2-599c-9f4e-437caf1a23ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-5415" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $4 \\times 7$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns. Find $\\textrm{rank}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $7$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n7-3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/key-prerequ